    "result": "The fix is complete. Here's a summary of what was done:\n\n## Summary\n\n**Issue:** Missing `.gitignore` in HTML Output Directory Causes Unintended Git Tracking\n\n**Solution:** Modified `/testbed/coverage/html.py` to automatically create a `.gitignore` file in the HTML output directory when generating reports.\n\n**Changes made to `/testbed/coverage/html.py`:**\n\n1. Added a new method `make_local_gitignore_file()` (lines 232-253) that:\n   - Creates a `.gitignore` file with content `/*` to ignore all contents\n   - Preserves any existing user content if the file already exists\n   - Appends `/*` only if not already present (prevents duplication)\n   - Handles edge cases like missing trailing newlines\n\n2. Called `make_local_gitignore_file()` at the end of the `report()` method (line 219), after static files are created.\n\n**Testing verified:**\n- All 46 existing HTML tests pass\n- `.gitignore` is correctly created with content `/*`\n- Existing user content is preserved when `.gitignore` already exists\n- Pattern is not duplicated on subsequent report generations\n- Files in the output directory are correctly ignored by Git",
